---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { withBase } from '../lib/paths';
---

<Layout title="Data privacy">
  <section class="relative overflow-hidden">
    <div class="bg-grid absolute inset-0"></div>
    <div class="relative mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-16 text-center sm:px-6 sm:py-24">
      <h1 class="text-glow text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight text-white sm:text-5xl">Data privacy</h1>
      <p class="mx-auto mt-4 max-w-xl text-brand-gray">
        What this site, the mod, and the app do and don't collect.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="mx-auto max-w-2xl px-4 pb-24 sm:px-6">
    <div class="space-y-8 rounded-2xl border border-white/10 bg-ink-900/60 p-6 text-sm text-brand-gray sm:p-10">
      <div>
        <h2 class="text-base font-semibold text-white">This website</h2>
        <p class="mt-2">
          This site is static: it sets no cookies, runs no analytics or tracking scripts, and doesn't collect
          anything from your visit. Contributor names and avatars shown on the Contributors page are pulled from
          GitHub's public API at build time, not from you visiting the site.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="text-base font-semibold text-white">The mod (server-side)</h2>
        <p class="mt-2">
          The mod runs entirely on the Minecraft server it's installed on. There is no third-party or Devsforge-
          operated service in the loop. Pairing stores your Minecraft player UUID, an authentication token, and
          the devices/groups you set up, on that server, under that server owner's control, the same way any other
          server-side mod's data would be stored. Nothing is sent anywhere else.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="text-base font-semibold text-white">The app</h2>
        <p class="mt-2">
          The app talks directly to the Minecraft server you pair it with, over the connection described in the
          <a class="text-brand-teal underline hover:text-teal-300" href={withBase('/wiki/developers')}>developer docs</a>.
          It does not send your data to Devsforge or any other third party. Push notifications are deferred (see the
          <a class="text-brand-teal underline hover:text-teal-300" href={withBase('/roadmap')}>roadmap</a>); if that
          changes, this page will be updated to reflect whatever that requires.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="text-base font-semibold text-white">Questions or deletion requests</h2>
        <p class="mt-2">
          Since your data lives on the Minecraft server you paired with, deletion is a matter of asking that
          server's owner to revoke your pairing (see the player wiki). For anything about this site or project
          specifically, reach out at
          <a class="text-brand-teal underline hover:text-teal-300" href="mailto:undeaD_D@live.de">undeaD_D@live.de</a>.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
